- {"name": "container_memory_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Current memory usage in bytes, including all memory regardless of when it was accessed"}
Question: Show the filesystem usage and limit bytes for all containers of the auth service.

Metrics List:
- {"name": "node_network_receive_errs_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Network device statistic receive_errs."}
- {"name": "container_network_transmit_errors_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Cumulative count of errors encountered while transmitting"}
- {"name": "container_network_receive_errors_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Cumulative count of errors encountered while receiving"}
- {"name": "node_forks_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Total number of forks."}
- {"name": "node_filesystem_device_error", "type": "gauge", "description": "Whether an error occurred while getting statistics for the given device."}
- {"name": "node_disk_reads_merged_total", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of reads merged."}
- {"name": "node_context_switches_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Total number of context switches."}
- {"name": "node_disk_writes_completed_total", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of writes completed successfully."}
- {"name": "node_disk_reads_completed_total", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of reads completed successfully."}
- {"name": "node_disk_read_bytes_total", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of bytes read successfully."}
Question: What is the total number of transmission errors for all pods of the assurance service on node k8s-node2 in the last 5 minutes?
